{"chunk_id": "7f62ec60d6d5", "text": "After the arrival of King Dasaratha in Mithila for the weddings of his sons, he performs lavish acts of charity, donating hundreds of thousands of richly adorned cows to the brahmins in their names. Bharata\u2019s maternal uncle Yudhajit arrives from the Kaikeya kingdom and is warmly received. The next day, the royal and sage assemblies gather in the marriage pavilion where Vasistha, Vishwamitra, and other rishis prepare the sacred fire and ritual implements. King Janaka formally offers his daughter Sita to Rama, declaring that she will accompany him in virtue and devotion. When Rama accepts her hand, the marriage is sanctified by Vedic rites. The moment is celebrated not only by those present but by the heavens themselves: divine music resounds and flowers rain from the sky, marking the sacred union of Rama and Sita.\nDasaratha gives vast charity, Janaka hosts the rites, and Sita is formally married to Rama before sages and the sacred fire.\nThemes: sacred marriage, ritual ceremony, royal duty and charity, family alliance, divine blessing", "vector": [0.009550800547003746, -0.022371966391801834, -0.014002501033246517, 0.005532923620194197, -0.02293260022997856, 0.009837791323661804, -0.038843926042318344, -1.2879147107014433e-05, -0.020049339160323143, -0.027577852830290794, -0.00467194989323616, 0.004191406536847353, -0.01417603064328432, 0.020543230697512627, -0.007581907324492931, 0.003770930925384164, 0.04263487830758095, -0.02633644826710224, 0.02824527397751808, -0.011513018980622292, -0.003395506413653493, -0.01669888384640217, -0.005993444472551346, 0.035666998475790024, -0.021918119862675667, 0.006677551195025444, 0.023106129840016365, -0.02413395792245865, 0.006060186307877302, -0.01978236995637417, -0.017980333417654037, -0.03361134231090546, -0.00403456250205636, -0.024414274841547012, -0.02569572441279888, 0.0035106365103274584, -0.0008472080226056278, -0.00416804663836956, 0.004608544986695051, -0.0132616637274622